SET temp_dir = NULL

FINALLY:
    IF temp_dir != NULL:
        DO Remove only this run's ADF output/temp directory; report cleanup errors.

CHECK mode == "publish"

CHECK The developer explicitly requested publishing this technical summary.

CHECK summary_exists == TRUE

CHECK saved_summary has a matching ticket ID and completed Summary content fields from
    ../technical-summary.md#summary-content, without placeholders or unsupported claims.
    Report missing/incomplete content without creating or rewriting the draft.

DO Resolve private absolute acli/ix under shared Inux guidance; report missing tools without
    setup/login/version probes. Follow the shared Jira execution rule for every Jira call.
    Consult only exact subcommand help when needed.

SHELL `{acli} jira workitem comment list --key {ticket_id} --json --paginate` AS comments_result

SET comments = JSON(stdout of comments_result)

DO Check comments for duplicates and material clarifications; record Booleans
    evidence_contradicts_summary and identical_comment, plus any duplicate URL.
    Never replace unrelated comments.

IF evidence_contradicts_summary == TRUE:
    ASK "Jira evidence contradicts the saved summary. Would you like to revise it?" AS revision_request

    STOP "Publication stopped because evidence contradicts the draft; the saved summary is unchanged."

IF identical_comment == FALSE:
    DO Read ../cli.md for ix ADF conversion; never build ADF manually.

    DO Create unique temp_dir; set absolute adf_path inside it.

    SHELL `{ix} adf {summary_path} {adf_path}` AS adf_result

    DO Inspect ADF for faithful saved-summary conversion.

    DO Immediately before posting, recheck ticket.md's active ID as current_ticket_id and
        compare the saved summary with saved_summary; record Boolean summary_is_unchanged.

    CHECK current_ticket_id == ticket_id

    CHECK summary_is_unchanged == TRUE

    SHELL `{acli} jira workitem comment create --key {ticket_id} --body-file {adf_path} --json` AS publish_result

    SET published = JSON(stdout of publish_result)

    DO Retain the returned comment/ticket URL; look it up only if missing. Inspect remote
        state before retrying uncertain writes. Leave task files unchanged.

ELSE:
    DO Retain identical comment URL/status for the reply; do not post again.

PRINT with the verified Jira URL or duplicate status, briefly; leave task files unchanged.
